# Copy to .env for a local run. `.env` is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# Quarkus reads this file at startup, so anything here overrides
# application.properties. Only what a developer actually needs is listed; the rest has a
# default that is either correct or explicitly a development convenience.

# --- Outgoing mail -------------------------------------------------------------
# Invitations and password resets. With nothing set, an invitation is still created and its
# link comes back to whoever asked for it — an instance with no relay must not be an instance
# where nobody can be given an account.
#
# The dev profile is already pointed at Resend: host smtp.resend.com, username "resend", and
# the API key as the password. The from address has to be on a domain Resend has verified.
# KEYDRA_MAIL_API_KEY=

# --- Encryption ----------------------------------------------------------------
# What encrypts every stored credential. The dev profile has a fixed development value, so
# this is only needed when you want a local instance to behave like a real one.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# KEYDRA_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Enforcement ---------------------------------------------------------------
# On by default, including in dev, where an admin/admin account is seeded so that costs
# nothing. Set it to false only for a machine nobody else can reach: it admits everybody who
# can open the address, with every permission.
# KEYDRA_SECURITY_ENABLED=true
